BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:FETISH: The Official Toronto Book Launch Party
DTSTART:20261122T180000
DTEND:20261122T180000
UID:b1f93838146edef2cb3467c3e6cc91cf@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join sex educator and author Niki Davis-Fainbloom for the offi
 cial launch of Fetish: Smash Taboos and Celebrate What Turns You On Join s
 ex educator and author Niki Davis-Fainbloom for the official Toronto launc
 h of Fetish: Smash Taboos and Celebrate What Turns You On—an immersive e
 vening exploring desire through storytelling\, science\, and playful surpr
 ises. The night will include: A short reading from Fetish and a playful\, 
 science-backed Q&amp\;A about what turns us on—and why Book signing and 
 mingling Interactive experiences to indulge your senses Pop-ups\, includin
 g Come As You Are with some sexy treats A sexy auction More surprises to d
 iscover throughout the night How does something completely ordinary become
  intensely erotic—and what can our most unusual turn-ons teach us about 
 desire? Drawing on hundreds of studies\, interviews\, and an original surv
 ey of 260 people\, Niki will take attendees on a scholarly romp into the w
 orld of unique desires and offer insights into what makes us all uniquely 
 weird—and therefore totally normal—humans. Whether you have a fetish\,
  love someone who does\, or are simply curious about the wonderfully weird
  ways people get turned on\, you’re invited to celebrate desire without 
 shame. // your host: Niki Davis-Fainbloom \\\\ Niki Davis-Fainbloom is a s
 ex educator\, writer\, and relationship coach. Her work sits somewhere bet
 ween science\, education\, and play. She has led more than 500 workshops f
 or audiences including Planned Parenthood\, NYU\, and the United Nations\,
  bringing research and practical tools to life through humor\, conversatio
 n\, and delightfully ridiculous activities. Niki holds a master’s degree
  in psychology from NYU and has studied sexuality at the Kinsey Institute.
  Her writing has appeared in Cosmopolitan\, Refinery29\, and Insider. Her 
 first book\, Fetish: Smash Taboos and Celebrate What Turns You On\, comes 
 out October 27\, 2026. Follow her on Instagram:@missbloomsexeducator. ‍
LOCATION:Book Bar\, 600 Markham St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/fetish-the-official-toronto-book-launch-pa
 rty
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
