BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fetish: The Science of What Turns Us On
DTSTART:20261123T190000
DTEND:20261123T190000
UID:9183a21d56f32a62f7d8a29e8a74c97a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:On Monday November 23\, 7-8:30PM Join us at Come As You Are at
  464 College Street with sex educator and author Niki Davis-Fainbloom for 
 a playful\, research-backed workshop inspired by her new book\, Fetish: Sm
 ash Taboos and Celebrate What Turns You On. Drawing on hundreds of studies
 \, interviews\, and an original survey of 260 people\, Niki explores how b
 iology\, conditioning\, and culture shape our erotic imaginations. Along t
 he way\, you’ll meet some of the book’s fascinating characters\, inclu
 ding a woman whose love of bicycles shaped her romantic life and a man who
  enjoys being wrapped in carpet and stepped on. Through storytelling\, gui
 ded reflection\, interactive discussions\, and a science-backed Q&amp\;A\,
  we’ll explore where desires come from\, why certain fantasies stick\, a
 nd how to approach our turn-ons with curiosity and less shame. Expect surp
 rising science\, practical communication tools\, and plenty of room for qu
 estions. Please register in advance! Come As You Are is an accessible spac
 e with a barrier-free entrance\, an automatic door\, and a wheelchair-acce
 ssible bathroom located on the main floor. No one will be turned away for 
 lack of funds. For further accommodation please contact lilin@comeasyouare
 .com. ‍
LOCATION:Come as You Are\, 464 College St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/fetish-the-science-of-what-turns-us-on
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:M. Butterfly
DTSTART:20261123T193000
DTEND:20261123T193000
UID:78c10b5dbd37ca78520c3ba037e4bcfe@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:David Cronenberg’s work has always had queer tendencies. Fro
 m his 1969 feature film STEREO onwards\, there’s been more fluid bodies\
 , unstable identities and allegorical depictions of the queer and trans ex
 perience than we can even list. So it felt like high time we celebrated Mr
 . Cronenberg\, especially given he’s also… inarguably the most iconic 
 Toronto filmmaker of all time. And we’re doing so with what might be his
  most overtly queer film (and definitely among his most divisive): 1993’
 s M. BUTTERFLY. Starring regular Cronenberg collaborator Jeremy Irons alon
 gside John Lone\, M BUTTERFLY adapts David Henry Hwang’s 1988 play\, whi
 ch is itself loosely based on the true story of the relationship between F
 rench diplomat Bernard Bouriscot and Chinese opera singer Shi Pei Pu. With
  lots to say about gender performance\, Western imperialism and even cultu
 ral revolution\, it’s certainly one of Cronenberg’s most explicitly po
 litical films\, in addition to being one of his queerest. So join us Novem
 ber 23rd at @paradiseonbloor for M BUTTERFLY\, and the opportunity to pick
  up a printed copy of this gorgeous poster by @hiredhandstudio. 🦋🦋
 🦋🦋🦋 ‍
LOCATION:Paradise Theatre\, 1006 Bloor Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/m-butterfly
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
