BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:yo yo oto presents: Daniel Bell
DTSTART:20261127T220000
DTEND:20261127T220000
UID:7daedcdc01d31473ecfbcbe8c3a29f15@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:yo yo oto presents... Daniel Bell Trustfall Hiroki ~~~~~~ Dani
 el Bell stands as one of electronic music’s most influential minimalists
 . Emerging from Detroit in the early 1990s\, Bell developed a radically st
 ripped-down language of rhythm\, repetition and funk that helped shape the
  course of minimal house and techno worldwide. As DBX\, he created a serie
 s of landmark recordings\, most notably 1994’s “Losing Control”—a 
 hypnotic underground anthem whose influence continues to resonate across g
 enerations of producers and DJs. Behind the decks\, Bell is a master of re
 duction: precise\, patient and relentlessly funky\, building dance floors 
 through subtle shifts rather than obvious gestures. More than three decade
 s into his career\, he remains one of the few Detroit originals still push
 ing minimal electronic music forward on his own unmistakable terms. Trustf
 all is a Toronto-based artist\, radio host and organizer. They have a soft
  spot for eclectic\, left-handed selections and oddball psychedelia across
  all genres. They organize a bi-monthly party series called Freakers Corne
 r at Bampot House in Toronto with their collective Freakers Union. These t
 wo will be joined by yo yo oto organizer and label head hiroki &lt\;3 :) D
 ate: Friday\, November 27 Location: 961 College St. *Venue has two stairca
 ses\; some accessibility arrangements can be made\, but washrooms are down
 stairs. ‍
LOCATION:The Jama\, 961 College St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/yo-yo-oto-presents-daniel-bell
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
